## C# 13 – The “Fine‑Tuning” of C# 13

| Feature | What it adds | Why it matters |
|---------|--------------|----------------|
| **Global Attributes** | An attribute can be applied to an entire assembly, namespace, or module via the `global` keyword, e.g., `global [assembly: System.Runtime.CompilerServices.TypeForwardedTo(typeof(Foo))]`. | Reduces repetition for cross‑assembly annotations such as `[assembly: InternalsVisibleTo]`. |
| **Required‑Member Defaults** | `required` fields and properties may now be initialized with a default value directly in the declaration, eliminating the need for a separate constructor. | Simplifies immutable data types that still need a default state. |
| **Record‑Struct Inheritance & Constructor Forwarding** | Record structs can now inherit from other record structs, and constructors can forward to base constructors with the `: base(...)` syntax. | Enables a richer type hierarchy for immutable value objects. |
| **Pattern‑Matching Enhancements** | • More sophisticated list patterns, including `..` capture and nested patterns.<br>• Support for `switch` expression exhaustiveness checking against union types.<br>• `and`/`or`/`not` patterns are fully integrated with relational and constant patterns. | Lets you write a single, expressive pattern that covers a wide range of scenarios. |
| **Interpolated‑String Handlers** | The handler API receives an extra `bool` parameter indicating whether the formatted result will be consumed (`true`) or discarded (`false`). | Allows more efficient formatting for scenarios where the output might be ignored. |
| **Static‑abstract Property Initializers** | Static abstract members can be initialized with expressions that reference other static abstract members. | Gives generic math APIs more expressive power (e.g., `static abstract T Zero { get; }`). |
| **Performance & Interoperability Tweaks** | • `ref` locals and returns can now be used in `foreach` on `Span<T>`. <br>• `IAsyncEnumerable<T>` now supports `ConfigureAwait(false)` in the `await foreach` statement. | Improves both runtime performance and async patterns. |

### Example: Global Attribute + Record‑Struct Inheritance

```csharp
// Global attribute that applies to every type in the assembly
global [assembly: System.Runtime.CompilerServices.SkipLocalsInit];

// Record struct inheriting from another
public record struct Money(decimal Amount, string Currency) : IComparable<Money>
{
    // Base constructor forwarded
    public Money(decimal amount) : this(amount, "USD") {}

    public int CompareTo(Money other) => Amount.CompareTo(other.Amount);
}

// Using a pattern with the new `not` and relational patterns
static void DisplayMoney(Money m) => m switch
{
    { Amount: > 0 } when m.Currency == "EUR" => Console.WriteLine($"Positive EUR: {m.Amount}"),
    not { Amount: 0 } => Console.WriteLine($"Non‑zero: {m.Amount} {m.Currency}"),
    _ => Console.WriteLine("Zero or unknown"),
};
```

